From ab1a6e974d720f53bbcc273e8bd312e0d7769f83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite-Emulator Dev <dev@auralite-emu.local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:19:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] U1 update

USB U1: BOT/CSW correctness.

The status channel is honest now (all measured against the guest's own
validator, AuraLite-OS@0ed0d29 drivers/usb/msc.c):
- dCSWTag echoes dCBWTag (the guest rejects mismatches with
  `CSW tag mismatch got/want`; the old model wrote 0).
- dCSWDataResidue is expected-minus-moved: measured on short data
  (expected 1024, one 512-byte qTD -> residue 512) and on an absent
  image (disk_len 0 -> residue 512).
- bCSWStatus distinguishes OK / FAILED (unsupported SCSI opcode: data
  phase moves nothing, residue stays) / PHASE (malformed CBW signature,
  and the next command stays in sync).
- Status-phase framing is BOT-shaped: the CSW is the 13-byte IN
  (measured: the sample firmware's status qTD token is 0x000D0180), so
  a cut-short data phase still settles residue.

tests/test_usb.c grows 2 -> 7 machine vectors driving QH/qTD chains
through the doorbell: tag echo, residue x2, FAILED, PHASE, and the
firmware-shaped negative control (tag=1, READ(10) LBA 0, data at
0x00100000, CSW at 0x00020200) -- the boot-integration gate strings do
not move (make test green).

Once-per-phase negative control (measured): reverting the tag echo
reddens exactly `ok csw tag echo` (assert r32r(c + 4) == tag, RC=134).

Teardown fix in the same patch: devices_done() calls pci_done() -- the
PCI device list leaked 11232 bytes / 36 allocations under LSan as soon
as a fixture built the full device set (measured by make test-sanitize;
now leak-clean).

Gate: make test + make test-sanitize green; docs synced (USB_PLAN U1
receipts, CHANGELOG 0037, ROADMAP queue).
